// STAGE 6 - FINALIZE (spec 4.6), 3.4's STAMP ON THE BUILT PRIM.
//   PRIMITIVE wrangle, precision 64.
//   input 0  the packed pieces out of `copy_packed`
//   input 1  CONFIG
//
// ⚠️ THIS NODE EXISTS BECAUSE NOTHING HAD EVER COMPARED THE STAMP.
// `place_packed_parity` measures `P` and the packed prim's world bounds, and
// it measures them at 0.0 m over 471 prims - so the branch was believed to
// reproduce the reference.  What it reproduced was the GEOMETRY.  Of 3.4's
// fourteen prim attributes the branch published nine, four were simply
// ABSENT (`pc_generated`, `pc_deformed`, `pc_corner_cut`, `pc_replaced`) and
// one was WRONG on every prim of a sectioned run (`pc_section`, the artist's
// section KEY as a float where `_stamp_values` writes the section INDEX as an
// int).  `place_stamp_parity` is the check; this is the fix.
//
// The four constants are not placeholders, they are what THIS BRANCH BUILT,
// and each one is only sound because of a property the graph enforces above:
//
//   pc_generated = 1   every prim here was made by polyChain (3.4).
//   pc_deformed  = 0   `copy_packed` is the PACKED branch. 13.9 N5's deform
//                      gate does not exist yet, so a piece the curvature
//                      budget WOULD unpack is not built here at all - it has
//                      no counterpart in the reference's packed set either,
//                      which is why the parity matches on `pc_elem_id` and
//                      skips what it cannot pair.
//   pc_corner_cut = 0  4.3 is not ported (N8) and the native plan therefore
//                      emits no piece carrying a cut. A case WITH corners is
//                      out of scope by name in `_place_out_of_scope`, not
//                      silently stamped 0 and compared.
//   pc_replaced  = 0   4.6's hero replacement is N7's other half; a case with
//                      overrides is out of scope by name for the same reason.
//
// When N5 and N8 land, the first two stop being constants and read the gate
// and the cut flag; the check that pairs them with the reference is already
// written, which is the point of landing it now.

i@pc_section    = i@_sec_out;
i@pc_generated  = 1;
i@pc_deformed   = 0;
i@pc_corner_cut = 0;
i@pc_replaced   = 0;

// ⚠️ AND `pc_style` IS THE STYLE'S ID, NOT THE CURVE'S STYLE KEY.  The two
// are different strings and the branch published the wrong one: 3.1's
// per-curve `pc_style` picks WHICH style out of a multi-style payload, while
// 3.4's `pc_style` is the id of the style that produced the element
// (`Placement.style_id`).  Carrying the plan point's `_style_key` through
// `copytopoints` read EMPTY on every case with a named style - 24 of them -
// against the reference's own id.  `pc_cfg["style_id"]` is the same string
// `pc_stamp` already hashes into `pc_elem_id`, so it is the one that is
// asserted bit-exact on 92 cases.
dict cfg = detail(1, "pc_cfg");
string style_id = "";
if (isvalidindex(cfg, "style_id")) { string v = cfg["style_id"]; style_id = v; }
s@pc_style = style_id;
